qrt{3}}{3}|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186354631 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186354635 :question/problem "Given that $B=[\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2} & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(B).$" "Given that $B=\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{2} & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(B).$"] [:db/cas 17592186354635 :que